1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,900
Some memories fade.

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:08,400
The person doesn't.

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:13,900
10 best tips to deal with Alzheimer's.

4
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:19,100
Tip 01 — Keep a calm, familiar routine

5
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:23,300
Same time, same place, same steps. Predictability quietly lowers confusion — and fear.

6
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:28,300
Tip 02 — Make home safe and simple

7
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:32,500
Nightlights, clear paths, a handrail where it matters. Remove the clutter, keep the dignity.

8
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:37,500
Tip 03 — Speak with warmth, not correction

9
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:41,700
Don't argue with the story — join it. One question at a time. A hand on theirs. Their name in your voice.

10
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:46,700
Tip 04 — Let music bring them back

11
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:50,900
A song from their twenties can open a door no question can. Keep the old records close.

12
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:55,900
Tip 05 — Move a little, every day

13
00:00:55,900 --> 00:01:00,100
A short walk, a stretch, a dance in the kitchen. Movement steadies mood, sleep and balance.

14
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:05,100
Tip 06 — Simplify the choices

15
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:09,300
Two shirts, not ten. Two options, not an open question. Independence survives on smaller decisions.

16
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:14,300
Tip 07 — Guard the meals and the water

17
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:18,500
Set the table, turn off the noise, offer water often. Thirst and hunger are forgotten early.

18
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:23,500
Tip 08 — Plan early — together

19
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,700
Money, medication, legal wishes, care preferences. Decide while their voice can still lead the room.

20
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:32,700
Tip 09 — Build a care team, then use it

21
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:36,900
You cannot be the whole circle. Respite care, support groups, siblings, neighbours. Let people help.

22
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:41,900
Tip 10 — Be patient with yourself

23
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:46,100
Some days will go backwards. That isn't failure — that's the disease. Your calm is still medicine.

24
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:49,580
There is no cure. Not yet.

25
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:52,480
But there is care.

26
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:53,980
There is patience.

27
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:55,480
And there is love.

28
00:01:57,780 --> 00:02:02,180
Share this with someone who cares for someone.

29
00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:03,180
Not medical advice. Always consult a qualified healthcare professional.
